# Discretionary access control
[module:DAC][policy:blocking_user_access_to_system_files]=Restrict user access to system files
[module:DAC][policy:custom_mode_and_owner]=Custom file permissions and owners
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_passwd_tries]=Number of authentication attempts
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_securepath]=List of directories searched for commands executed through sudo
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_timeout]=Time between sudo launches in minutes before the password is requested again
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_require_authentication]=Require authentication when executing commands through sudo
[module:DAC][policy:systemcommandlock]=Restrict system commands for users

[module:DAC][policy:blocking_user_access_to_system_files][description]=Sets secure permissions for system files, primarily configuration files. The following files and permissions will be used:
    /etc/bashrc root:root 0644
    /etc/crontab root:root 0600
    /etc/fstab root:root 0640
    /etc/hostname root:root 0644
    /etc/hosts root:root 0644
    /etc/hosts.allow root:root 0644
    /etc/hosts.deny root:root 0644
    /etc/group  root:root 0644
    /etc/ntpd.conf root:ntp 0640
    /etc/resolv.conf root:root 0644
    /etc/sysctl.conf root:root 0644
    /etc/logrotate.conf root:root 0644
    /etc/inittab root:root 0644
    /etc/passwd root:root 0644
    /etc/shadow root:shadow 0640
    /etc/sudoers root:root 0440
    /etc/grub.cfg root:root, 0600
    /etc/sysconfig/securetty root:root  0600
[module:DAC][policy:custom_mode_and_owner][description]=Allows setting a custom list of files and directories for which FIC will check and fix the owner, group, and access mode. Specify one rule per line in the format: /path|owner|group|mode. The path must be absolute, and the mode must be a 3- or 4-digit octal value. Example:
    /etc/example.conf|root|root|0644
    /opt/app/private|root|fic|0750
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_passwd_tries][description]=Number of authentication attempts
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_securepath][description]=Description
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_timeout][description]=Time between sudo launches in minutes before the password is requested again
[module:DAC][policy:sudo_require_authentication][description]=Replaces local NOPASSWD rules with PASSWD and prevents authentication from being disabled in active sudoers files. Existing sudo timestamps, PAM, and external LDAP/SSSD sources are out of scope.
[module:DAC][policy:systemcommandlock][description]=Restrict system commands for users


