[module:OSS][policy:disable_autologin][description]=Disable automatic login
[module:OSS][policy:screenlock_timeout][description]=Screen lock timeout
[module:OSS][policy:disable_videodisplay_when_locked][description]=In the SDDM display manager, the name of the enabled video adapter is shown on the lock screen by default.
[module:OSS][policy:lock_on_tty_switch]=Lock screen when switching to another terminal
[module:OSS][policy:lock_on_tty_switch][description]=This policy is not supported yet. If enabled, applying it fails instead of reporting a false success.
[module:OSS][policy:lock_on_tty_switch][message:not_implemented]=Locking the screen on TTY switch is not implemented yet
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_tmp_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /tmp entry in /etc/fstab. The optimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,noexec,relatime. The minimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,relatime. Already mounted filesystems are not remounted automatically.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_var_tmp_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /var/tmp entry in /etc/fstab. The optimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,noexec,relatime. The minimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,relatime. Already mounted filesystems are not remounted automatically.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_dev_shm_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /dev/shm entry in /etc/fstab. The optimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,noexec,mode=1777. The minimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,mode=1777.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_home_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /home entry in /etc/fstab. The optimal profile enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,relatime. The strict profile additionally adds noexec.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_removable_media_profile][description]=For /media, /mnt, and /run/media entries in /etc/fstab. The optimal profile enforces nodev,nosuid,noexec. The strict profile additionally adds ro.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_var_log_secure_options][description]=Requires a dedicated /var/log entry in /etc/fstab and enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,noexec,relatime.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_var_log_audit_secure_options][description]=Requires a dedicated /var/log/audit entry in /etc/fstab and enforces rw,nodev,nosuid,noexec,relatime.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_boot_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /boot entry in /etc/fstab. The minimal profile enforces nodev,nosuid,noexec. The optimal profile additionally adds ro.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_boot_efi_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /boot/efi entry in /etc/fstab. The minimal profile enforces nodev,nosuid,noexec,umask=0077. The optimal profile additionally adds ro.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_srv_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /srv entry in /etc/fstab. The minimal profile enforces nodev,nosuid. The optimal profile additionally adds noexec.
[module:OSS][policy:fstab_opt_profile][description]=Requires a dedicated /opt entry in /etc/fstab and enforces nodev. ro is not enforced because /opt/fic contains FIC runtime data: configuration, logs, the device database, and service files.

Some desktop environments support global settings, for example MATE
Others use per-user settings, for example KDE
Where possible, a lock against modification is applied

